  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish whether the core multimodal hypothesis holds and provide a reference point for the remaining 9 experiments. config_003 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) tests the central question—does combining RNA and image modalities with multiprofile aggregation improve classification accuracy—using moderate-cost components (ResNet-50, average pooling, PCA) that avoid committing to the most expensive encoders (ViT-L, transformer aggregation, scGPT) before we know the direction. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can escalate to ViT-L, transformer aggregation, or scGPT/scVI encoders to push accuracy higher. If it underperforms, the result localizes the problem (e.g., fusion strategy, encoder quality) and guides targeted follow-ups. Expected relative cost: moderate—roughly 1.5–2× a single-profile unimodal baseline due to multiprofile processing and dual-modality forward passes, but well below the ViT-L + transformer + multiprofile configurations (configs 001/007/020) which would be ~3–4× this cost. This makes it the most information-per-GPU-hour choice for experiment 1."
}

